cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "The Invisible Snitch: exact capture of a fleeing invisible target"
authors:
  - name: "The invisible-snitch contributors"
date-released: 2026-11-20
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >
  For the invisible-Snitch pursuit problem, an explicit path fixed in advance sees every
  starting direction by time 13.1 d whenever the Snitch's speed is at most 5.8e-3, for every
  vision radius; consequently a single path catches the Snitch exactly. Proofs checked by
  AI referees and audits, not yet by a human.
